Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T11:53:12-08:00","id":318401,"title":"","content":"I am a professional humanities-major-surrounded-entirely-by-STEM-people. <br /> <br /> The details change, but that remains constant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T14:53:01-08:00","id":320204,"title":"","content":"I'm currently teaching French as Second Language (FSL) to public servants (CBSA to be more specific). I've been FSL for more then 11 years, hoping to get a permanent position at one point though.<br /> <br /> I'm also doing Translation and Marketing for a Start-up social media business (XAHIVE). We're doing pretty good for somethnig that launched in August. Already having a few big player looking at us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T19:37:22-08:00","id":321316,"title":"","content":"I have been working for a big bank as a personal banker since July. I really enjoy my work so far. Before that I soent 12 years in retail, mostly selling but also managing. I hated that place.<br /> As far as my career goals, it depends. I can see myself being pretty happy at my bank for a long time, and there seems to be upward mobility. <br /> Dream job? Go to grad school, get my PhD in History and teach college. A guy can hope right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T01:24:46-08:00","id":321557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=321316#post321316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dream job? Go to grad school, get my PhD in History and teach college. A guy can hope right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm right there with you! Although Classical Literature and Philosophy also appeal to me :P Nevertheless, like you, I love my profession and since business is starting to flourish I can probably quit doing &quot;debt law&quot; and centre on my favourite areas which would be Heaven!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T02:13:27-08:00","id":321593,"title":"","content":"I am President and CEO of my own company named Ravenous Press. I have a few employees, we are small right now, but I am looking to hire writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T02:01:23-08:00","id":337890,"title":"","content":"Software Development, we produce Scientific Research Data Management Software, used in everything from (bizzarely) bed sales (it does their inventory management by repurposing our systems) to getting sattelites into orbit, fine chemical production, biological assays and supports the whole drug development lifecycle. I work in performance mostly so endless reams of HTTP calls, fighting websocket upgrades, bewildering duplication of redundant calls and graphs, oh so many graphs. Most of our tooling is open source or bespoke so I do a bit of building our own capability too.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't change much, except maybe a chance to do some more coding to build some more tools or tweak the ones we have, but deadlines aren't moving to let me do that.<br /> <br /> We're switching to agile in the new year and I'm not looking forward to looking after the performance of a dozen different teams each running on their own independent code streams and them looking after them again once they smush them together into a giant fustercluck to release <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T15:50:02-08:00","id":349371,"title":"","content":"Poor Social Work grad student. What is money?<br /> <br /> Oh right that thing I need to pay my student loans later on. Crap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T15:54:45-08:00","id":349372,"title":"","content":"You live in USA or UK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T20:08:20-08:00","id":349484,"title":"","content":"Engineering student though I should have graduated already. I keep changing my mind, was Mechanical, then switched to Nuclear, then back to Mechanical. Probably explains why I like Exalted so much because crunching systems are piss easy to understand.<br /> <br /> I've done some fun internships so far. I can safely tell you that the people who make cars have no idea what they're doing half the time and hate their jobs. I can also tell you why Nuclear energy is so out of date in terms of technology. Also feel free to ask why I hate Linux distros from the 90's and Fortran.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T21:00:42-08:00","id":351285,"title":"","content":"I get an allowance from my husband. My full time job doesn't pay. But it does mean our daughter isnt in day care.<br /> I don't really plan on doing anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T00:33:47-08:00","id":353550,"title":"","content":"I exchange &quot;favors&quot; for money from my fiance,does that count as a job? haha <br /> <br /> But seriously, i dont currently have a job, and wont for at least a few years. But i'd like to go back into cashier or customer service work I really enjoy it, despite my terrible people skills and my utter hatred of most other humans. I find something awfully enjoyable about helping other people with their technical issues or what not.<br /> <br /> <br /> My fiance works at a call center for a bank handling collections, he's the guy who call when you owe the bank money. He gets to be an asshole and gets paid well to do it and even has the option for promotion and career growth which is nice. He hasnt figured out what he wants to do yet, but is quite happy with his job","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T06:44:29-08:00","id":353672,"title":"","content":"For a past-time I'm a research student in psychology, with a particular focus on narrative psychology.<br /> <br /> For money, I trade. Mostly shares, but I've been known to dabble in many areas, such as books, currency, and in one memorable case toy soldiers (albeit with help from a friend who was into that and gave me some good advice).<br /> <br /> My life is freaking sweet. I can spend all day in the living room in my pyjamas eating microwave noodles and not only be &quot;productive&quot;, but make more than people who actually perform productive labour for a living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=349484#post349484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done some fun internships so far. I can safely tell you that the people who make cars have no idea what they're doing half the time and hate their jobs. I can also tell you why Nuclear energy is so out of date in terms of technology. Also feel free to ask why I hate Linux distros from the 90's and Fortran.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that (the nuclear out of date thing)? I have a passing interest in nuclear energy, but it's been nearly 10 years since I studied physics, so a lot of the technical stuff is really hard for me to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T13:22:51-08:00","id":354034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=353672#post353672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is that (the nuclear out of date thing)? I have a passing interest in nuclear energy, but it's been nearly 10 years since I studied physics, so a lot of the technical stuff is really hard for me to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a hobby-horse of mine, and it's more political than technical.<br /> <br /> The technical side is easy enough. It's a high capital industry with a very large amount of regulation. This results in a very long life cycle, where you might only be building a new reactor for a given area every 20-30 years (that's a quick turnover). Because you want things to be at least somewhat standardized (makes it easier to get employees, and decreases mistakes of the &quot;but we did it that way over there&quot; variety) you have a solid reason to have them work in the same old ways. Add on to that the fact that companies really don't like to buy expensive new infrastructure before they absolutely have to, and that life cycle of 2-3 decades can get stretched to 4-5 decades.<br /> <br /> On the regulation front and the political front (they tie together) you get the FUD factor hitting hard. Media plays up the horrific nature of a disaster, people believe it, get concerned to hysterical, political action tighten regulations in response, you get more violations of the regulations that goes back to feeding the machine. And this also plays into the &quot;Well, we know how these old style reactors work, so they're safer!&quot; viewpoint.<br /> <br /> The end result is that what we actually use to generate power is about 3 generations behind the current prototype designs that various educational bodies have produced, but the educational bodies can't get the capital to produce commercial scale reactors to prove out the technology, and that's assuming they could even get the ability to build it in the first place with public opinion being &quot;nuclear power plant = unexploded bomb&quot; and &quot;experimental nuclear power plant = THEY'RE GIVING US CANCER FROM AN UNEXPLODED BOMB!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T15:05:18-08:00","id":354119,"title":"","content":"Umm...Japan? Should have scared everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T15:40:56-08:00","id":354135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=354119#post354119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm...Japan? Should have scared everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. When a reactor designed and built over 50 years ago encounters earthquakes and tsunami beyond it's rated capacity goes boom there are problems. And then the biggest issue it has is the cesium it released when it broke.<br /> <br /> The deliberately &quot;adjusted&quot; safety studies and surveys made by the owner to keep the plant operational certainly didn't help with the reliability issues.<br /> <br /> Apart from that we have a lot of land classed as contaminated and deemed unsuitable due to the radiation being from a man-made source... a level of radiation that's lower than living in Denver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T16:17:49-08:00","id":354155,"title":"","content":"*nods* I get that...I understand the whole of it. But there is nothing that can be made accident-proof. Japan's PM was in favor of building more reactors before the accident. And the public there was all for it. Afterwards, he did a 180 and wants nothing to do with them. And neither does the public. And all it took was one accident. And that's my point. One. Accident. Contamination of everything, food, land, water, everything. They can't be certain of the cancer rates now, they never bothered with such trivialities before. But if I remember reading earlier, there are over a 100 thyroid cancer cases in children now that they pretty much attribute to Fukushima.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T21:18:07-08:00","id":354415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=354155#post354155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* I get that...I understand the whole of it. But there is nothing that can be made accident-proof. Japan's PM was in favor of building more reactors before the accident. And the public there was all for it. Afterwards, he did a 180 and wants nothing to do with them. And neither does the public. And all it took was one accident. And that's my point. One. Accident. Contamination of everything, food, land, water, everything. They can't be certain of the cancer rates now, they never bothered with such trivialities before. But if I remember reading earlier, there are over a 100 thyroid cancer cases in children now that they pretty much attribute to Fukushima.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhhh no. The cancer rates are a range the same as they always are, and they're not certain about it because because the potential increase in the number of cancer deaths is so tiny it's within the margin of error for estimating cancer rates in a population. The OUTSIDE estimate is in the range of 130 deaths, and that's using a method of calculation that has since been discredited as producing results that are inaccurately high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T23:00:12-08:00","id":354505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uK367T7h6ZY\" data-code=\"uK367T7h6ZY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/uK367T7h6ZY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T08:52:15-08:00","id":354762,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah the molten salt reactors. There's also uranium variants and the basic design goes back to the 50's. They're actually kind of cool, both in tech and history... it was a molten reactor that the US was experimenting with sticking onto bomber aircraft back before ICMBs took over as the weapon of choice. Unfortunately they couldn't get the radiation shielding light enough to protect the pilots for the weeks they'd be spending in the things so gave it up.<br /> <br /> Like all tech, they've got drawbacks. Power output is a lower than with your standard US reactors or the CANDU variants, and the big headache is the molten salt is corrosive as all get out, and we have limited experience with it outside of some test reactors and solar power plants that use molten salts. The liquid cores also require regular cleaning, but that's more an operations headache than anything.<br /> <br /> There's also a uranium pile &quot;battery&quot; design that has been floating around and periodically getting refined since the 70's. It's pretty much the ultimate in low-end passive power generation... IIRC the japanese were working on a standardized version, there were one or two put into isolated towns up in Alaska a few years back and the gates foundation recently starting throwing several million at some engineers that were working on a variant. They put out a constant charge for a couple decades without anything high pressure or complex... to the point where you just bury them and let them provide the power for a town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T09:02:35-08:00","id":354781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=354415#post354415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhhh no. The cancer rates are a range the same as they always are, and they're not certain about it because because the potential increase in the number of cancer deaths is so tiny it's within the margin of error for estimating cancer rates in a population. The OUTSIDE estimate is in the range of 130 deaths, and that's using a method of calculation that has since been discredited as producing results that are inaccurately high.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, irrelevant to what people believe.<br /> And believe me, if it were your child that suddenly came down with thyroid cancer (in a family with zero history of it) and you lived nearby the accident site you wouldn't be arguing. (and you know what I just did there. That's the argument your fighting. Or do you honestly believe that Japan wants to hear it now? No. They don't.)<br /> <br /> Accidents happen. That's why they're called &quot;accidents.&quot; And considering how widespread the damage and the potential lethality for generations to come, not one person wants to be near one when it does. (and where does the waste go? Yes, that's a leading question. You already know the answer. Burying the stuff isn't the best way to go here, neither is paying off some Third World country to take it off another country's hands)<br /> <br /> And this is Fukushima. There isn't much to argue in Russia. The environment there is a catastrophe waiting to happen again and again. They can't afford the upgrades and neither can they afford to shut their reactors down. And when the crap blows up again, (I'm fairly certain it is a matter of &quot;when&quot; not &quot;if&quot;) it won't matter how you calculate the numbers, Europe as a whole isn't going to be happy.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, we'll just have to agree that we're in disagreement here. (I live about 50 miles or so from Three Mile Island. And I still think I'm too close to it. When that accident hit, I was still a kid, but I recall my parents talking about moving.)<br /> <br /> Science needs another direction to go in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:38:45-08:00","id":355184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=354781#post354781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Accidents happen. That's why they're called &quot;accidents.&quot; And considering how widespread the damage and the potential lethality for generations to come, not one person wants to be near one when it does. (and where does the waste go? Yes, that's a leading question. You already know the answer. Burying the stuff isn't the best way to go here, neither is paying off some Third World country to take it off another country's hands)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression they've made some pretty big strides in that area over the last ten years or so? I mean, it's still a major problem, I'm sure, but the fact that progress has been made implies more progress can be made. And if we can, somehow, fix that issue, surely that's one of the major stumbling blocks addressed (the other being safety, which seems to be a more political issue than a scientific or engineering one)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T12:09:06-08:00","id":355949,"title":"","content":"Nuclear generators are under constant scrutiny and going through innovation after innovation. The problem is that many of those innovations go underutilized because of all the red tape that is involved in getting a new reactor built, not to mention the cost. At this point, if Lockheed is onto something with their fusion reactor they went all hype about, fission reactors will be a thing of the past, as no new ones will be built in favor of lockheed's design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T13:44:02-08:00","id":356012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starmage21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/312649-what-do-you-do-for-money?p=355949#post355949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuclear generators are under constant scrutiny and going through innovation after innovation. The problem is that many of those innovations go underutilized because of all the red tape that is involved in getting a new reactor built, not to mention the cost. At this point, if Lockheed is onto something with their fusion reactor they went all hype about, fission reactors will be a thing of the past, as no new ones will be built in favor of lockheed's design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I read into it in detail, and while cool, it is very hype. It's a compact research reactor that (if it works exactly as expected and everything is tested at maximum speed) would decrease the time it takes to iterate the research they are doing from years to months... assuming they can dramatically scale up the data analysis they're doing.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it's good and is what will hopefully be a step forward. It's just something that got overhyped and then media kinda ran with it turning &quot;compact fast experimental research equipment&quot; into &quot;production ready compact fusion in a decade!!!11!!!one!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T21:49:13-08:00","id":356265,"title":"","content":"For money? I make people provoke micro-injuries in their muscles and extend their muscles and mobilize their joints beyond what they are used to. I punch, kick and throw people and make they do the same to others. And I stab people with multiple needles.<br /> <br /> In other words, I'm a personal trainer, I teach martial arts and I'm an acupuncturist ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":